From: Firmware Security Follow-up <security@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] f2fs wait for checkpoint before reading nat flags

Acquire the retained node_write read semaphore before nat_tree_lock and release in reverse order, excluding checkpoint block_operations through unblock_operations. Use existing f2fs_down_read/up_read, including this branch's CONFIG_F2FS_UNFAIR_RWSEM behavior. The newer upstream *_trace wrappers also add optional priority adjustment and tracing and call these semaphore primitives once each; their lock context, priority and tracing framework is absent here and is not imported. The original fixture supplied those unavailable APIs and masked the missing prerequisite. The corrected complete node.c and every other changed production C unit now compile against real captured ARM64 headers. No structure or configuration change.

CVE: CVE-2026-53017
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/238e14eb7226f883b72caccd2d37bf5707df066b]

--- a/fs/f2fs/node.c
+++ b/fs/f2fs/node.c
@@ -428,6 +428,7 @@
 	struct nat_entry *e;
 	bool need_update = true;
 
+	f2fs_down_read(&sbi->node_write);
 	f2fs_down_read(&nm_i->nat_tree_lock);
 	e = __lookup_nat_cache(nm_i, ino, false);
 	if (e && get_nat_flag(e, HAS_LAST_FSYNC) &&
@@ -435,6 +436,7 @@
 			 get_nat_flag(e, HAS_FSYNCED_INODE)))
 		need_update = false;
 	f2fs_up_read(&nm_i->nat_tree_lock);
+	f2fs_up_read(&sbi->node_write);
 	return need_update;
 }
 
